  "text": "In the twelfth month we returned, most of all, to the \"national defense authorization\" — 38 of us on the fourth, and 36 that same day naming the \"national defense authorization act.\" A version of the fuller phrase, \"the national defense authorization,\" we trace in the record to Michael F. Bennet. We said it in its longer forms too, and as \"national defense authorization act ndaa\"; the count held near two dozen and above across the variants. It was, by the numbers, the thing we were most together on.\n\nThen, on the seventeenth, we turned. 24 of us spoke of \"relations with cuba\"; 21 of \"the cuban people\"; 21, again, \"of alan gross.\" The record shows two convergences in one month — one on the authorization, one on Cuba — and we note, without comment, that both fell on single days.",
